Z||000000||FieroMaster88||01-05-2001||01:52 AM||||I know this makes me sound like a rice boy, but I am getting a Honda CRX this week for $100. They sell these J-spec (japan spec) engine kits for pretty cheap. I know a place for about $500 I can get a new Engine, Trans, wire harness and computer! Probably a 1.6L Vtec. If I do it right (no stickers, no big ass spoiler) i can get the car into the 13's easy. <P>What does everyone think.  I have always kinda been into import tuning, want to open my own shop, imports and Fiero's, probably in Ohio.  I will be ASE Certified in another year too.  Would I get any business from people here?  Hey, at least it is not a MR2!!!<P>Later<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1_1.jpg"> <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||01-05-2001||02:08 AM||||put it in a Del Sol instead... looks way better than a CRX IMHO...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>but the del sols really need wings.. something tasteful..<P>and for the record, I'd gladly buy an MR2, but you couldn't pay me to drive a CRX......<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
