Z||000003||GT Bastard||01-05-2001||08:18 AM||||I think 13's might be wishful thinking.  If you ever browse import mags, even the forced-induction riceboys are running high 14's.  Those Jap motors aren't THAT much better.  I believe the B16A2 makes 145hp.  But you've still got nothing for torque.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||01-05-2001||09:29 AM||||My concern is if any $100 CRX unibody is going to be roadworthy. I say for the $ if you wind up with a streetable package, you're doing fine, no matter what it is. Go for it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||01-05-2001||09:54 AM||||Hey, a steal is a steal. No flames from this corner. Best of luck.<P>Raydar ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroMaster88||01-05-2001||03:59 PM||||Well, I dont care much for the CRX either, but for $100 I have no complaignts.  It only needs a clutch.  I would drive it until spring so I dont keep racking up miles on the Fiero!  Then engine swap time!  I met a guy in Ohio who got a Jspec engine and put it in his CRX (pos like the one I am lookig at) and it ran 13's no problem, with the same engine I am talking about.  I will find out today if the guy is gonna sell it to me or not.  I will keep everyone posted.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1_1.jpg"> <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
